  "text": "Why do two yellow round peas produce wrinkled green offspring? In 1866, Gregor Mendel crossed yellow round peas with green wrinkled ones. Every first-generation child was yellow and round! But the green trait didn’t vanish—it was hiding. In the F2 generation, alleles recombined into a sixteen-cell matrix. Nine yellow round, three green round, three yellow wrinkled, and one lone green wrinkled pea. That nine-to-three-to-three-to-one ratio proved genes sort independently.",
